        {
          "id": 1035082240,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "I would argue, that #18219 takes precedence over increasing verbosity. Also, the fact, that increasing verbosity only really matters, if the user wants it, but if he wants to determine the fact in a scripting environment (and my guess is, that would be one of the use-cases), just printing the error message does not help him there, together with the fact that verbosity is decreased anyhow in such scenarios.\n\nSo tl;dr not sure if theses the right move here.",
          "author": {
            "id": 2498449,
            "username": "rknall",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Roland Knall",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/9e1d973c5007651b2ca47071f80324c2de5349d873e365cf0761df5542dfe382?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/rknall"
          },
          "created_at": "2022-07-22T08:53:28.239Z",
          "updated_at": "2022-07-22T08:53:28.239Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 167092470,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
