        {
          "id": 1035616359,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "I haven't used `editcap` enough to wrap my head around what seems like inverse logic:\n> By default the selected packets with those numbers will not be written to the capture file.\n\nAdd in timestamps and it gets more confusing. There also seems to be a bug in `unix_epoch_to_nstime` which allows invalid timestamps that should generate an error.  \n  \n```\n        case 'A':\n        case 'B':\n        {\n            nstime_t in_time;\n\n            check_startstop = TRUE;\n            fprintf(stderr, \"iso8601_to_nstime: %d\\n\", iso8601_to_nstime(&in_time, ws_optarg, ISO8601_DATETIME));\n            fprintf(stderr, \"unix_epoch_to_nstime: %d\\n\", unix_epoch_to_nstime(&in_time, ws_optarg));\n            \n            if ((0 < iso8601_to_nstime(&in_time, ws_optarg, ISO8601_DATETIME)) || (0 < unix_epoch_to_nstime(&in_time, ws_optarg))) {\n```\n\n```\nC:\\Development\\wsbuild64_2022>run\\RelWithDebInfo\\editcap.exe -V -A 2005-09-06T01:22:21 -B 2005-09-06T01:22:22 p:\\wap_google.pcap split\niso8601_to_nstime: 19\nunix_epoch_to_nstime: 4\niso8601_to_nstime: 19\nunix_epoch_to_nstime: 4\nFile p:\\wap_google.pcap is a Wireshark/tcpdump/... - pcap capture file.\nPacket: 2\nPacket: 3\nPacket: 4\nTotal selected: 3\n\nC:\\Development\\wsbuild64_2022>run\\RelWithDebInfo\\editcap.exe -V -A 2005-09-06T01:22:21 -B 2005-09-06 p:\\wap_google.pcap split\niso8601_to_nstime: 19\nunix_epoch_to_nstime: 4\niso8601_to_nstime: 0\nunix_epoch_to_nstime: 4\neditcap: start time is after the stop time\n```\n\nFor me at least, if I'm using verbose mode to figure out the `editcap` syntax for a certain range of packets, more info is better. But I also don't use `editcap` often so happy to close this MR to clean up the backlog.  \n\n```\n    4 Warning(s)\n    0 Error(s)\n\nTime Elapsed 00:01:18.07\n\nC:\\Development\\wsbuild64_2022>msbuild /m /p:Configuration=RelWithDebInfo Wireshark.sln\n\nC:\\Development\\wsbuild64_2022>\nC:\\Development\\wsbuild64_2022>run\\RelWithDebInfo\\editcap.exe -V -r -c 2 p:\\wap_google.pcap split\nFile p:\\wap_google.pcap is a Wireshark/tcpdump/... - pcap capture file.\nTotal selected: 0\n\nC:\\Development\\wsbuild64_2022>run\\RelWithDebInfo\\editcap.exe -V -r -c 2 p:\\wap_google.pcap split 1 3\nFile p:\\wap_google.pcap is a Wireshark/tcpdump/... - pcap capture file.\nAdd_Selected: 1\nNot inclusive ... 1\nAdd_Selected: 3\nNot inclusive ... 3\nPacket: 1\nPacket: 3\nTotal selected: 2\n\nC:\\Development\\wsbuild64_2022>run\\RelWithDebInfo\\editcap.exe -V -r -c 2 p:\\wap_google.pcap split 1-3\nFile p:\\wap_google.pcap is a Wireshark/tcpdump/... - pcap capture file.\nAdd_Selected: 1-3\nInclusive ... 1, 3\nPacket: 1\nPacket: 2\nContinuing writing in file split_00001_20050906012221\nPacket: 3\nTotal selected: 3\n\nC:\\Development\\wsbuild64_2022>run\\RelWithDebInfo\\editcap.exe -V  -c 2 p:\\wap_google.pcap split 1-3\nFile p:\\wap_google.pcap is a Wireshark/tcpdump/... - pcap capture file.\nAdd_Selected: 1-3\nInclusive ... 1, 3\nPacket: 4\nTotal selected: 1\n\nC:\\Development\\wsbuild64_2022>run\\RelWithDebInfo\\editcap.exe -V  -c 2 p:\\wap_google.pcap split\nFile p:\\wap_google.pcap is a Wireshark/tcpdump/... - pcap capture file.\nPacket: 1\nPacket: 2\nContinuing writing in file split_00001_20050906012221\nPacket: 3\nPacket: 4\nTotal selected: 4\n\nC:\\Development\\wsbuild64_2022>run\\RelWithDebInfo\\editcap.exe -V -r -c 2 p:\\wap_google.pcap split\nFile p:\\wap_google.pcap is a Wireshark/tcpdump/... - pcap capture file.\nTotal selected: 0\n\n********************* (bad? timestamp - no error)\n\nC:\\Development\\wsbuild64_2022>run\\RelWithDebInfo\\editcap.exe -V -A 2005-09-06 p:\\wap_google.pcap split\nFile p:\\wap_google.pcap is a Wireshark/tcpdump/... - pcap capture file.\nPacket: 1\nPacket: 2\nPacket: 3\nPacket: 4\nTotal selected: 4\n\n********************* (bad? timestamp - no error)\n\nC:\\Development\\wsbuild64_2022>run\\RelWithDebInfo\\editcap.exe -V -A 2005-09-07 p:\\wap_google.pcap split\nFile p:\\wap_google.pcap is a Wireshark/tcpdump/... - pcap capture file.\nPacket: 1\nPacket: 2\nPacket: 3\nPacket: 4\nTotal selected: 4\n\n\n\nC:\\Development\\wsbuild64_2022>run\\RelWithDebInfo\\editcap.exe -V -A 2005-09-07T00:00:00 p:\\wap_google.pcap split\nFile p:\\wap_google.pcap is a Wireshark/tcpdump/... - pcap capture file.\nTotal selected: 0\n\nC:\\Development\\wsbuild64_2022>run\\RelWithDebInfo\\editcap.exe -V -A 2005-09-06T00:00:00 p:\\wap_google.pcap split\nFile p:\\wap_google.pcap is a Wireshark/tcpdump/... - pcap capture file.\nPacket: 1\nPacket: 2\nPacket: 3\nPacket: 4\nTotal selected: 4\n\nC:\\Development\\wsbuild64_2022>run\\RelWithDebInfo\\editcap.exe -V -A 2005-09-06T00:00:00 p:\\wap_google.pcap split\n\nC:\\Development\\wsbuild64_2022>run\\RelWithDebInfo\\editcap.exe -V -A 2005-09-07T00:00:00 -B 2005-09-06 p:\\wap_google.pcap split\neditcap: start time is after the stop time\n\nC:\\Development\\wsbuild64_2022>run\\RelWithDebInfo\\editcap.exe -V -A 2005-09-07T00:00:00 -B 2005-09-06T00:00:00 p:\\wap_google.pcap split\neditcap: start time is after the stop time\n\nC:\\Development\\wsbuild64_2022>run\\RelWithDebInfo\\editcap.exe -V -A 2005-09-06T00:00:00 -B 2005-09-06T00:00:00 p:\\wap_google.pcap split\nFile p:\\wap_google.pcap is a Wireshark/tcpdump/... - pcap capture file.\nTotal selected: 0\n\nC:\\Development\\wsbuild64_2022>run\\RelWithDebInfo\\editcap.exe -V -A 2005-09-06T00:00:00 -B 2005-09-07T00:00:00 p:\\wap_google.pcap split\nFile p:\\wap_google.pcap is a Wireshark/tcpdump/... - pcap capture file.\nPacket: 1\nPacket: 2\nPacket: 3\nPacket: 4\nTotal selected: 4\n\nC:\\Development\\wsbuild64_2022>run\\RelWithDebInfo\\editcap.exe -V -A 2005-09-06T00:00:00 -B 2005-09-06T01:22:00 p:\\wap_google.pcap split\nFile p:\\wap_google.pcap is a Wireshark/tcpdump/... - pcap capture file.\nTotal selected: 0\n\nC:\\Development\\wsbuild64_2022>run\\RelWithDebInfo\\editcap.exe -V -A 2005-09-06T00:00:00 -B 2005-09-06T01:23:00 p:\\wap_google.pcap split\nFile p:\\wap_google.pcap is a Wireshark/tcpdump/... - pcap capture file.\nPacket: 1\nPacket: 2\nPacket: 3\nPacket: 4\nTotal selected: 4\n\nC:\\Development\\wsbuild64_2022>run\\RelWithDebInfo\\editcap.exe -V -A 2005-09-06T00:00:00 -B 2005-09-06T01:22:20 p:\\wap_google.pcap split\nFile p:\\wap_google.pcap is a Wireshark/tcpdump/... - pcap capture file.\nTotal selected: 0\n\nC:\\Development\\wsbuild64_2022>run\\RelWithDebInfo\\editcap.exe -V -A 2005-09-06T00:00:00 -B 2005-09-06T01:22:21 p:\\wap_google.pcap split\nFile p:\\wap_google.pcap is a Wireshark/tcpdump/... - pcap capture file.\nPacket: 1\nTotal selected: 1\n\nC:\\Development\\wsbuild64_2022>run\\RelWithDebInfo\\editcap.exe -V -A 2005-09-06T01:22:21 -B 2005-09-06T01:22:21 p:\\wap_google.pcap split\nFile p:\\wap_google.pcap is a Wireshark/tcpdump/... - pcap capture file.\nTotal selected: 0\n\nC:\\Development\\wsbuild64_2022>run\\RelWithDebInfo\\editcap.exe -V -A 2005-09-06T01:22:21 -B 2005-09-06T01:22:22 p:\\wap_google.pcap split\nFile p:\\wap_google.pcap is a Wireshark/tcpdump/... - pcap capture file.\nPacket: 2\nPacket: 3\nPacket: 4\nTotal selected: 3\n\nC:\\Development\\wsbuild64_2022>\n```",
